<<~ ahu #/head>>

! K17-R ~ one lease law on the realm boards

Order (controller, 2026-10-22): Wave D (<<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/k15-wave-d-lane">>) runs BEFORE this lane. Circles and identities now travel to every device of a face, which raises the stakes of the omnibus node key.

Wave C made a PersonaGroup's lease epoch rise only on a signed advance (`lease-advance`, `lares persona lease`) and built the fleet board's signed frontier. K17-R extends both laws to the Nexus and cabal-realm boards, as its own lane cut after Wave C lands (<<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/k15-wave-c-lane">>). It shares only the readers Wave C built: `hand-lineage`, the quorum act and `readWideningFrontier`.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/the-mandate>>

!! The mandate (operator rulings on forks 3 and 4, 2026-10-22)

* ''One lease law.'' Every lease epoch rises only on a signed advance. A face advances by a per-writer signed slot under its KEL lineage. A Nexus or cabal-realm advance signs as a `QuorumAct` at the roster's threshold under its own epoch's lineage.
* ''The unsigned max-register retired entirely''; the signed path stands alone, and a census (`lease-law-census.test.ts`) refuses its names and any lease-prefix scan that names no signed reader.
* ''The realm boards' frontiers widen K17 the same way the fleet board's do.''

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/the-slices>>

!! The five slices, one lane landed whole

# ''R1 ~ the mesh format ~ BUILT.'' `quorum-lease.ts`: one `QuorumAct` per advance under `QUORUM_LEASE_DOMAIN`, a content-addressed slot beside the face's per-writer slots, read under `charterHandLineage` (`makeHandLineage` bound to the seal-epoch chain, so an older epoch's advance verifies under the keys of its own epoch and a forged chain reads no hand). The fold is monotone (the verified maximum only climbs, so no sighting un-stales a cut grant).
# ''R2 ~ the writer on held seats ~ BUILT.'' The `nexus-rekey` verb resolves the resource's own charter (`lease-charter.ts`: a Nexus AID, or a realm through the Nexus its ledger names), takes the held seats at the threshold (`selectHeldQuorumSigners`) and lands the advance through `rollQuorumLeaseOnBoard`. Fewer held seats refuse by name; the vessel's atom signs nothing here.
# ''R3 ~ the readers ~ BUILT.'' The herm's raise door (`leaseEpochOnBoard`, null where no lineage verifies, so a raise never stands against a fence that cannot read), `cabalAdmissionEpoch` in `cabal-join` and `cabal-vouch`, and the vessel standing read signed advances only. A join that would admit waits (`incomplete-view`) where the realm's lineage reads none; a refusal narrows and needs no lineage. The realm clock's fold no longer borrows the retired register; the realm FEED stays its own liveness heartbeat under its own seal law (`cabal-realm#/the-tie-break`), never an authority epoch.
# ''R4 ~ the retirement ~ BUILT.'' The unsigned register, its writer and its readers left; fixtures moved onto `seatedCharter` and held seats.
# ''R5 ~ the realm boards' frontiers ~ BUILT for the charter quorum hand.'' `realm-frontier.ts` rides the shared hand frontier (`fleet-frontier.ts`): the quorum signs genesis and each successor, a quorum act registers its raise in the same board change (`edge-kapae-cmd`, `edge-cosign`), and a vouch founds the genesis on first touch where this vessel holds the threshold of seats. The shadow ring reads `RealmFold.frontier`: `memberAside` answers aside and `standsInRealm` false where no frontier qualifies; `cabal-join` waits as `frontier-unknown` before an admission and names the head it acted under (`frontier.asOf`).

!!! Owed
* The voucher hands' own frontier on a realm board (holder acts register nothing).
* A seal roll leaves the realm head at the older epoch (`stale-lineage`, closed) until a quorum act, a seated vouch or a cosign signs a head under the new epoch; the roll anchor does not yet register one.
* A split-seat cosign carries edge signatures alone: a vessel below the threshold lands the act without a frontier, so readers wait until a seat holder registers one.
* A closed roster's keys can still raise the lease (stale more, never less) until the recovery door (K18) closes that window; the fold never lowers.
* A realm admit bundle carrying its board's frontier and snapshot.

Reds: an unsigned advance on a realm raises nothing and a threshold hand raises it (`quorum-lease.test.ts`, `lease-rekey.test.ts`); a sub-threshold hand raises nothing; an older epoch's advance verifies under its own epoch's keys and a forged lineage refuses; a realm reader before any qualifying frontier waits as unknown and acts as of it after (`realm-frontier.test.ts`, `edge-shadow-ring.test.ts`); the census proves itself on a planted site.

<<~/ahu>>

